+### Landing site sync
+
+Every successful `main` build that produces all five advertised installers now
+publishes an automatic, pinned pre-release (`v<package-version>-build.<run-number>`).
+The release job reads the published
+asset metadata back from GitHub, then refreshes the marked download block in
+this README with direct URLs, exact sizes and SHA-256 values. It also asks
+`cambuz-landing` to verify the same release and update its public download page.
+
+[`docs/landing-content.json`](docs/landing-content.json) is the reviewed
+machine-readable source for the landing Features page. When a PR adds or changes
+a user-visible feature, update this file alongside the README and tests. CI
+validates the contract before a release is allowed; the downstream site copies it
+only after the assets are public. Use an existing `screenshotId` when a genuine
+landing screenshot already exists, or omit it so the site shows a placeholder.
+
 Contributions are welcome — please open an issue first for anything beyond a small fix,
 and keep changes covered by `npm test`. No new release or signing automation is produced
 by this documentation; publishing is a maintainer decision tracked in DEVELOPMENT.md.
